  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "Marvin the Martian is mapped as the 'enemy' elected by Americans",
  "description": "The text 'they elect their enemy to rule over them' explicitly maps the visual entity Marvin the Martian (a known enemy character from Looney Tunes) onto the role of 'enemy' in the political context. The meme uses Marvin's villainous persona and his iconic weapon (rocket launcher) to symbolize a political adversary, creating an analogical mapping where the cartoon character represents the political enemy being elected by Americans. This mapping is reinforced by Marvin's disdainful expression and pose, which visually embody the contempt expressed in the text.",
